4. Master the core distributed-system concepts

I would make these your foundation layer.

A. Scalability:
              Understand:              
                            Vertical scaling
                            Horizontal scaling
                            Load balancing
                            Partitioning
                            Sharding
                            Replication
                            Caching
                            CDN
                            Stateless services
B. Consistency:
              
              Understand:              
                            Strong consistency
                            Eventual consistency
                            Read-your-writes
                            Monotonic reads
                            Quorum

Then understand why distributed systems often have to trade consistency for availability/latency.

C. Reliability:
              Understand:
                            Timeout
                            Retry
                            Exponential backoff
                            Circuit breaker
                            Bulkhead
                            Idempotency
                            Failover
                            Replication
                            Health checks
                            Dead-letter queues

D. Distributed coordination:
                     Eventually learn:
                            Leader election
                            Distributed locks
                            Logical clocks
                            Consensus
                            Raft
                            Paxos — conceptual level

You don't need to implement Paxos from scratch initially.

You need to understand what problem consensus solves.
